<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.10.4: Using the Standard Form of an Equation to Find the <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis>- and <emphasis effect="italics">y</emphasis>-intercepts</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01910</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.10.4: Using the Standard Form of an Equation to Find the X- and Y-Intercepts</md:title>
    <md:uuid>395ce4a5-cb02-477b-89d5-e33632ae1bab</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>

<para id="para-00001">The equations <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> both define the same quadratic function.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00002">Without graphing, identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph. Explain how you know.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00004"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>,<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>; The constants in the factors of an equation in factored form give a clue about where the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts are when the equation is graphed. In the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00005">Without graphing, identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of the graph. Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00006">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00007">8; The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph can be seen when the equation is in standard form. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate is the number without the variable. In the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, it is the 8 so the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
